# Preserve unlisted files exactly, including arbitrary embedded assets.
# Known text formats are normalized to LF on every platform.
#
# `* -text` disables every line-ending conversion, so a file whose format is
# not listed below keeps whatever bytes it has on disk and Git compares them
# raw. On a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true that means a CRLF copy is
# reported as modified forever, even when the committed content is identical.
# Every text format the project authors therefore belongs in one of the lists
# below; fixtures that must stay byte-exact stay unlisted on purpose.
* -text
*.go text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=lf
*.mod text eol=lf
*.sum text eol=lf
*.c text eol=lf
*.cc text eol=lf
*.cpp text eol=lf
